  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "The section has a cohesive, polished defense-console aesthetic: strong headline hierarchy, restrained cyan/green/yellow accents, consistent mono labels, clean borders, and responsive restructuring that remains composed at all three sizes. It falls short of demo-ready polish because mobile supporting text and metadata are extremely small and low-contrast, precedent rows become overly tall and sparse, and the global header visibly clips its horizontal navigation at tablet/mobile with no clear overflow affordance. Desktop also leaves an unusually large empty upper-right field, weakening balance.",
    "fix": "Make the header navigation intentionally scrollable with a visible edge fade or compact mobile menu; raise mobile metadata/body text size and contrast; tighten mobile row spacing; and rebalance the desktop hero by widening or repositioning the explanatory artifact block.",
